"requestId\":\"req_011CVTotVDvqReYGLWxx3DCH\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"c4e3caeb-7858-4b7b-b518-dff4922fa32d\",\"timestamp\":\"2025-11-25T02:21:12.731Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"c4e3caeb-7858-4b7b-b518-dff4922fa32d\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/alyshialedlie/.claude\",\"sessionId\":\"4373d577-5c18-44b5-b6fe-76676ebe2274\",\"version\":\"2.0.31\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01TUgzshsLEuwtcZPHT4mZgq\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01Vde4ccCLE7fMgAm4cxCDvm\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/alyshialedlie/.claude/hooks/post-tool-use-tracker.sh\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":53281,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":53281,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":6,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CVTotVDvqReYGLWxx3DCH\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"729d2349-1b15-4f6e-b4df-a4078610e031\",\"timestamp\":\"2025-11-25T02:21:13.714Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"729d2349-1b15-4f6e-b4df-a4078610e031\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/alyshialedlie/.claude\",\"sessionId\":\"4373d577-5c18-44b5-b6fe-76676ebe2274\",\"version\":\"2.0.31\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Vde4ccCLE7fMgAm4cxCDvm\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→#!/bin/bash\\n     2→set -e\\n     3→\\n     4→# Source performance monitoring\\n     5→source \\\"$(dirname \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\\")/lib/performance-monitor.sh\\\"\\n     6→perf_start \\\"post-tool-use-tracker\\\"\\n     7→\\n     8→# Post-tool-use hook that tracks edited files and their repos\\n     9→# This runs after Edit, MultiEdit, or Write tools complete successfully\\n    10→\\n    11→\\n    12→# Read tool information from stdin\\n    13→tool_info=$(cat)\\n    14→\\n    15→\\n    16→# Extract relevant data\\n    17→tool_name=$(echo \\\"$tool_info\\\" | jq -r '.tool_name // empty')\\n    18→file_path=$(echo \\\"$tool_info\\\" | jq -r '.tool_input.file_path // empty')\\n    19→session_id=$(echo \\\"$tool_info\\\" | jq -r '.session_id // empty')\\n    20→\\n    21→\\n    22→# Skip if not an edit tool or no file path\\n    23→if [[ ! \\\"$tool_name\\\" =~ ^(Edit|MultiEdit|Write)$ ]] || [[ -z \\\"$file_path\\\" ]]; then\\n    24→    perf_end \\\"skipped-not-edit-tool\\\"\\n    25→    exit 0  # Exit 0 for skip conditions\\n    26→fi\\n    27→\\n    28→# Skip markdown files\\n    29→if [[ \\\"$file_path\\\" =~ \\\\.(md|markdown)$ ]]; then\\n    30→    perf_end \\\"skipped-markdown\\\"\\n    31→    exit 0  # Exit 0 for skip conditions\\n    32→fi\\n    33→\\n    34→# Create cache directory in project\\n    35→cache_dir=\\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/tsc-cache/${session_id:-default}\\\"\\n    36→mkdir -p \\\"$cache_dir\\\"\\n    37→\\n    38→# Function to detect repo from file path\\n    39→detect_repo() {\\n    40→    local file=\\\"$1\\\"\\n    41→    local project_root=\\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\\\"\\n    42→\\n    43→    # Remove project root from path\\n    44→    local relative_path=\\\"${file#$project_root/}\\\"\\n    45→\\n    46→    # Extract first directory component\\n    47→    local repo=$(echo \\\"$relative_path\\\" | cut -d'/' -f1)\\n    48→\\n    49→    # Common project directory patterns\\n    50→    case \\\"$repo\\\" in\\n    51→        # Frontend variations\\n    52→        frontend|client|web|app|ui)\\n    53→            echo \\\"$repo\\\"\\n    54→            ;;\\n    55→        # Backend variations\\n    56→        backend|server|api|src|services)\\n    57→            echo \\\"$repo\\\"\\n    58→            ;;\\n    59→        # Database\\n    60→        database|prisma|migrations)\\n    61→            echo \\\"$repo\\\"\\n    62→            ;;\\n    63→        # Package/monorepo structure\\n    64→        packages)\\n    65→            # For monorepos, get the package name\\n    66→            local package=$(echo \\\"$relative_path\\\" | cut -d'/' -f2)\\n    67→            if [[ -n \\\"$package\\\" ]]; then\\n    68→                echo \\\"packages/$package\\\"\\n    69→            else\\n    70→                echo \\\"$repo\\\"\\n    71→            fi\\n    72→            ;;\\n    73→        # Examples directory\\n    74→        examples)\\n    75→            local example=$(echo \\\"$relative_path\\\" | cut -d'/' -f2)\\n    76→            if [[ -n \\\"$example\\\" ]]; then\\n    77→                echo \\\"examples/$example\\\"\\n    78→            else\\n    79→                echo \\\"$repo\\\"\\n    80→            fi\\n    81→            ;;\\n    82→        *)\\n    83→            # Check if it's a source file in root\\n    84→            if [[ ! \\\"$relative_path\\\" =~ / ]]; then\\n    85→                echo \\\"root\\\"\\n    86→            else\\n    87→                echo \\\"unknown\\\"\\n    88→            fi\\n    89→            ;;\\n    90→    esac\\n    91→}\\n    92→\\n    93→# Function to get build command for repo\\n    94→get_build_command() {\\n    95→    local repo=\\\"$1\\\"\\n    96→    local project_root=\\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\\\"\\n    97→    local repo_path=\\\"$project_root/$repo\\\"\\n    98→\\n    99→    # Check if package.json exists and has a build script\\n   100→    if [[ -f \\\"$repo_path/package.json\\\" ]]; then\\n   101→        if grep -q '\\\"build\\\"' \\\"$repo_path/package.json\\\" 2>/dev/null; then\\n   102→            # Detect package manager (prefer pnpm, then npm, then yarn)\\n   103→            if [[ -f \\\"$repo_path/pnpm-lock.yaml\\\" ]]; then\\n   104→                echo \\\"cd $repo_path && pnpm build\\\"\\n   105→            elif [[ -f \\\"$repo_path/package-lock.json\\\" ]]; then\\n   106→                echo \\\"cd $repo_path && npm run build\\\"\\n   107→            elif [[ -f \\\"$repo_path/yarn.lock\\\" ]]; then\\n   108→                echo \\\"cd $repo_path && yarn build\\\"\\n   109→            else\\n   110→                echo \\\"cd $repo_path && npm run build\\\"\\n   111→            fi\\n   112→            return\\n   113→        fi\\n   114→    fi\\n   115→\\n   116→    # Special case for database with Prisma\\n   117→    if [[ \\\"$repo\\\" == \\\"database\\\" ]] || [[ \\\"$repo\\\" =~ prisma ]]; then\\n   118→        if [[ -f \\\"$repo_path/schema.prisma\\\" ]] || [[ -f \\\"$repo_path/prisma/schema.prisma\\\" ]]; then\\n   119→            echo \\\"cd $repo_path && npx pris"
