              "size": 1395151,
              "ext": "jsonl",
              "preview": "{\"type\":\"summary\",\"summary\":\"Cloudflare Pages CI/CD Setup Complete, Billing Issue\",\"leafUuid\":\"9206e999-66a0-4dc5-bba2-31b257028aee\"}\n{\"type\":\"file-history-snapshot\",\"messageId\":\"0777bfd8-4576-460d-a446-ae30498c907d\",\"snapshot\":{\"messageId\":\"0777bfd8-4576-460d-a446-ae30498c907d\",\"trackedFileBackups\":{},\"timestamp\":\"2025-11-19T19:56:54.089Z\"},\"isSnapshotUpdate\":false}\n{\"parentUuid\":null,\"isSidechain\":false,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/alyshialedlie/code/ISPublicSites/IntegrityStudio.ai\",\"sessionId\":\"4a392c65-2fa2-4c43-b022-63a7ba78042e\",\"version\":\"2.0.31\",\"gitBranch\":\"feature/cloudflare-deployment\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"how do I solve this recuring error between my macos local build environment and linux deployment environment in a sustainable way for package dependancies? Run npm ci\\n  npm ci\\n  shell: /usr/bin/bash -e {0}\\nnpm error code EBADPLATFORM\\nnpm error notsup Unsupported platform for @rollup/rollup-darwin-arm64@4.53.2: wanted {\\\"os\\\":\\\"darwin\\\",\\\"cpu\\\":\\\"arm64\\\"} (current: {\\\"os\\\":\\\"linux\\\",\\\"cpu\\\":\\\"x64\\\"})\\nnpm error notsup Valid os:   darwin\\nnpm error notsup Actual os:  linux\\nnpm error notsup Valid cpu:  arm64\\nnpm error notsup Actual cpu: x64\\nnpm error A complete log of this run can be found in: /home/runner/.npm/_logs/2025-11-19T06_00_12_213Z-debug-0.log\\nError: Process completed with exit code 1.\\n\"},\"uuid\":\"0777bfd8-4576-460d-a446-ae30498c907d\",\"timestamp\":\"2025-11-19T19:56:54.078Z\",\"thinkingMetadata\":{\"level\":\"high\",\"disabled\":false,\"triggers\":[]}}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"0777bfd8-4576-460d-a446-ae30498c907d\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/alyshialedlie/code/ISPublicSites/IntegrityStudio.ai\",\"sessionId\":\"4a392c65-2fa2-4c43-b022-63a7ba78042e\",\"version\":\"2.0.31\",\"gitBranch\":\"feature/cloudflare-deployment\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_018Yn3frxoF5uqdAtsyVDqLg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The user is experiencing a common npm platform-specific dependency issue where they're developing on macOS (darwin/arm64) but deploying to Linux (linux/x64). The error shows that `@rollup/rollup-darwin-arm64` is being installed in their local environment and then causing issues in CI/CD because Linux can't use macOS-specific binaries.\\n\\nThis is a classic problem with `package-lock.json` getting platform-specific optional dependencies. When you run `npm install` on macOS, npm includes the macOS-specific optional dependencies in package-lock.json. Then when CI runs `npm ci` (which strictly follows package-lock.json), it tries to install those macOS-specific packages on Linux and fails.\\n\\nThere are several sustainable solutions:\\n\\n1. **Use `--omit=optional` or `--no-optional` flag in CI** - This tells npm to skip optional dependencies entirely. This works because platform-specific packages are usually marked as `optionalDependencies`.\\n\\n2. **Configure npm to only install platform-specific packages** - Use `.npmrc` with `optional=false` or configure npm to skip optional deps.\\n\\n3. **Regenerate package-lock.json in a platform-neutral way** - Delete package-lock.json and node_modules, then regenerate on a platform that matches your CI, or use Docker to generate it.\\n\\n4. **Use npm's built-in platform filtering** - Modern npm versions should handle this automatically, but if using an older version, upgrade.\\n\\n5. **Update to latest npm** - Newer versions of npm handle optional platform-specific dependencies better.\\n\\nThe most sustainable and recommended approach is:\\n\\n**Option 1**: Modify the CI workflow to use `npm ci --omit=optional` or add an `.npmrc` file to the project.\\n\\n**Option 2**: If they need some optional dependencies, they could delete and regenerate package-lock.json on a Linux machine or in Docker.\\n\\nLet me provide a comprehensive answer with the best sustainable solutions.\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":9,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":58043,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":58043,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CVHqYX9QfQoP5GkfhwqNV\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"e91b2edf-dc70-4865-bd24-0f9bceda8762\",\"timestamp\":\"2025-11-19T19:57:08.810Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"e91b2edf-dc70-4865-bd24-0f9bceda8762\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/alyshialedlie/code/ISPublicSites/IntegrityStudio.ai\",\"sessionId\":\"4a392c65-2fa2-4c43-b022-63a7ba78042e\",\"version\":\"2.0.31\",\"gitBranch\":\"feature/cloudflare-deployment\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_018Yn3frxoF5uqdAtsyVDqLg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This is a common issue where platform-specific optional dependencies from your macOS development environment end up in `package-lock.json` and break Linux CI builds.\\n\\n## Sustainable Solutions\\n\\n### **Recommended: Configure CI to Skip Optional Dependencies**\\n\\nSince `@rollup/rollup-darwin-arm64` is an optional platform-specific package, modify your CI workflow to skip optional dependencies:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":9,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":58043,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":58043,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CVHqYX9QfQo"
